ASSISTANT `prelude/config.nix` settles the last structural questions. What it confirms:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - `get-config` **exports** `DEVTOOLS_CONFIG` (per-tool dir under the gitignored `private/` root) and creates it with `mkdir -p` before the wrapper continues. So it's writable at launch time and is already where provider API keys live — the natural home for user keys: `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/users/<user>.key`.
ASSISTANT - Since it's exported and the wrapper `exec`s litellm, the authenticator inherits it. I'll still have the wrapper set a dedicated `LITE_LLM_USERS_DIR` (one line) so the Python side doesn't depend on the prelude's variable naming.
ASSISTANT - The `private/` gitignore handling in the prelude already covers the key files — no extra VCS hygiene needed.
