ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## 1. `lite-llm/config.nix` — users as objects
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Users become an attrset of submodules. The submodule is empty for now, but gives per-user options (rate limits, etc.) a place to land later without changing the configuration shape:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   # This submodule configures a user that is allowed to
ASSISTANT   # authenticate against the llm-lite instance. No options are
ASSISTANT   # defined yet; the submodule exists so that per-user settings
ASSISTANT   # (e.g. rate limits) can be added later. The authentication key
ASSISTANT   # is deliberately not an option: keys are generated at launch
ASSISTANT   # time and never enter the nix store.
ASSISTANT   user-spec = types.submodule { options = { }; };
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT and inside `spec`:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT       users = mkOption {
ASSISTANT         type = types.attrsOf user-spec;
ASSISTANT         default = { };
ASSISTANT         description = ''
ASSISTANT           The users that are allowed to authenticate against this
ASSISTANT           lite-llm instance, keyed by user name. Authentication keys
ASSISTANT           are generated when the instance is launched and are stored
ASSISTANT           in the tool's private configuration directory; they are not
ASSISTANT           part of this configuration. User names are used as file
ASSISTANT           names for the keys, so they must be file-name-safe.
ASSISTANT         '';
ASSISTANT       };
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## 2. `lite-llm/setup.nix`
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **a. User names** (attrset keys drive everything; validated since they become filenames):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   user-names =
ASSISTANT   let
ASSISTANT     names = lib.attrNames lite-llm.users;
ASSISTANT     invalid = lib.filter (name: builtins.match "[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*" name == null) names;
ASSISTANT   in
ASSISTANT     if invalid == [ ]
ASSISTANT     then names
ASSISTANT     else throw "lite-llm user names must be file-name-safe, invalid: ${toString invalid}"
ASSISTANT   ;
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **b. Authenticator** — subclasses litellm's `CustomAuth` base class, the supported custom-auth interface in 1.89.0 (the proxy instantiates the class and calls `auth(token)`, bool return = pass/fail):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   custom-auth = pkgs.writeText "custom_auth.py" ''
ASSISTANT     import os
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     from litellm.integrations.custom_auth import CustomAuth
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     USERS = ${builtins.toJSON user-names}
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     class UserKeyAuth(CustomAuth):
ASSISTANT         def auth(self, token: str) -> bool:
ASSISTANT             users_dir = os.environ.get("LITE_LLM_USERS_DIR", "")
ASSISTANT             if not token or not users_dir:
ASSISTANT                 return False
ASSISTANT             for user in USERS:
ASSISTANT                 try:
ASSISTANT                     with open(os.path.join(users_dir, user + ".key")) as key_file:
ASSISTANT                         if key_file.read().strip() == token:
ASSISTANT                             return True
ASSISTANT                 except OSError:
ASSISTANT                     continue
ASSISTANT             return False
ASSISTANT   '';
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Only names are embedded today; when per-user options exist, they can flow into this module the same way. Embedding the names means removing a user revokes their access even if the key file lingers.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **c. YAML** — enable the authenticator only when users are configured:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   lite-llm-config = {
ASSISTANT     model_list = lib.attrValues (lib.mapAttrs to-model-config lite-llm.models);
ASSISTANT   } // lib.optionalAttrs (lite-llm.users != { }) {
ASSISTANT     general_settings.custom_auth = "custom_auth.UserKeyAuth";
ASSISTANT   };
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **d. Config bundle** (authenticator must sit next to the YAML; litellm resolves the module relative to the config file's directory):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   lite-llm-config-dir = pkgs.runCommand "litellm-config-${lite-llm-name}" {} ''
ASSISTANT     mkdir -p "$out"
ASSISTANT     cp "${lite-llm-config-yml}" "$out/config.yml"
ASSISTANT     cp "${custom-auth}" "$out/custom_auth.py"
ASSISTANT   '';
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **e. Key generation** — create-once semantics, so keys are reused across launches:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   to-user-key-setup = user: ''
ASSISTANT   if [[ ! -f "$users_dir/${user}.key" ]]; then
ASSISTANT     ${pkgs.openssl}/bin/openssl rand -hex 32 > "$users_dir/${user}.key"
ASSISTANT     chmod 600 "$users_dir/${user}.key"
ASSISTANT     echo "Generated the authentication key of '${user}': $users_dir/${user}.key"
ASSISTANT   fi
ASSISTANT   '';
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT   users-setup =
ASSISTANT     if user-names == [ ]
ASSISTANT     then ""
ASSISTANT     else ''
ASSISTANT     users_dir="$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/users"
ASSISTANT     mkdir -p "$users_dir"
ASSISTANT     export LITE_LLM_USERS_DIR="$users_dir"
ASSISTANT     ${lib.concatStrings (map to-user-key-setup user-names)}
ASSISTANT     ''
ASSISTANT   ;
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **f. Launch script** — insert `${users-setup}` after `${api-key-setup}` (add a step 3 for user keys to its doc comment) and point at the bundle:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
