ASSISTANT No more files needed — that's everything I require. Two notes on what the new files settle:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - `examples/flakeModule.nix` shows the instance shape (`prelude-lite-llm`), so verification can be done by adding `users` there.
ASSISTANT - `flake.lock` pins nixpkgs at `e2587ca…`, but the litellm version isn't readable from the lock itself. I've written the authenticator against litellm's current documented custom-auth interface (a class with `auth(token) -> bool`). If your build turns out to predate class-based auth, the fix is pointing `custom_auth` at a module-level function instead — one word in the YAML. If you want certainty up front: `nix eval github:NixOS/nixpkgs/e2587caef70cea85dd97d7daab492899902dbf5d#python3Packages.litellm.version`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Here's the implementation:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## 1. `lite-llm/config.nix` — add `users` to `spec`
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT       users = mkOption {
ASSISTANT         type = types.listOf (types.strMatching "[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*");
ASSISTANT         default = [ ];
ASSISTANT         description = ''
ASSISTANT           The users that are allowed to authenticate against this lite-llm
ASSISTANT           instance. Authentication keys are generated when the instance is
ASSISTANT           launched and are stored in the tool's private configuration
ASSISTANT           directory; they are not part of this configuration. User names
ASSISTANT           are used as file names for the keys, so they are restricted to
ASSISTANT           file-name-safe characters.
ASSISTANT         '';
ASSISTANT       };
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## 2. `lite-llm/setup.nix` — five changes
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **a. Authenticator** (new binding, near `to-model-config`):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   /**
ASSISTANT   A litellm custom authenticator that validates the bearer token of
ASSISTANT   each request against the keys of the users defined in the
ASSISTANT   configuration. Keys are stored in the tool's configuration
ASSISTANT   directory, one file per user, under the directory pointed to by
ASSISTANT   the 'LITE_LLM_USERS_DIR' environmental variable, which is
ASSISTANT   exported by the launch script.
ASSISTANT   */
ASSISTANT   custom-auth = pkgs.writeText "custom_auth.py" ''
ASSISTANT     import os
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     USERS = ${builtins.toJSON lite-llm.users}
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     class CustomAuth:
ASSISTANT         def auth(self, token: str) -> bool:
ASSISTANT             users_dir = os.environ.get("LITE_LLM_USERS_DIR", "")
ASSISTANT             if not token or not users_dir:
ASSISTANT                 return False
ASSISTANT             for user in USERS:
ASSISTANT                 try:
ASSISTANT                     with open(os.path.join(users_dir, user + ".key")) as key_file:
ASSISTANT                         if key_file.read().strip() == token:
ASSISTANT                             return True
ASSISTANT                 except OSError:
ASSISTANT                     continue
ASSISTANT             return False
ASSISTANT   '';
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Embedding `USERS` means removing a user from the config revokes their access even if their key file lingers in `private/`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **b. Enable it in the YAML** (extend `lite-llm-config`):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   lite-llm-config = {
ASSISTANT     model_list = lib.attrValues (lib.mapAttrs to-model-config lite-llm.models);
ASSISTANT   } // lib.optionalAttrs (lite-llm.users != [ ]) {
ASSISTANT     general_settings.custom_auth = "custom_auth.CustomAuth";
ASSISTANT   };
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **c. Bundle YAML + authenticator in one directory** (litellm resolves the module relative to the config file's directory):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   lite-llm-config-dir = pkgs.runCommand "litellm-config-${lite-llm-name}" {} ''
ASSISTANT     mkdir -p "$out"
ASSISTANT     cp "${lite-llm-config-yml}" "$out/config.yml"
ASSISTANT     cp "${custom-auth}" "$out/custom_auth.py"
ASSISTANT   '';
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **d. Key generation** (new bindings next to `to-api-key-setup`):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   to-user-key-setup = user: ''
ASSISTANT   if [[ ! -f "$users_dir/${user}.key" ]]; then
ASSISTANT     ${pkgs.openssl}/bin/openssl rand -hex 32 > "$users_dir/${user}.key"
ASSISTANT     chmod 600 "$users_dir/${user}.key"
ASSISTANT     echo "Generated the authentication key of '${user}': $users_dir/${user}.key"
ASSISTANT   fi
ASSISTANT   '';
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT   users-setup =
ASSISTANT     if lite-llm.users == [ ]
ASSISTANT     then ""
ASSISTANT     else ''
ASSISTANT     users_dir="$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/users"
ASSISTANT     mkdir -p "$users_dir"
ASSISTANT     export LITE_LLM_USERS_DIR="$users_dir"
ASSISTANT     ${lib.concatStrings (map to-user-key-setup lite-llm.users)}
ASSISTANT     '';
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **e. Launch script** — add `${users-setup}` after `${api-key-setup}` (and a step 3 for user keys in its doc comment), and change the config path:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
